From e9e97900d659855d44cfb39e232aae891fa923dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:41:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 103/114] core: make the shared 3GPP enumerations public

External atom drivers need the call, network-registration, operator,
CLIP/CNAP and access-technology enumerations, which oFono keeps private
in src/common.h. Move the definitions into the public headers, where
Sailfish also puts them, and leave src/common.h defining its old
unprefixed constant names as aliases so in-tree code is untouched.

The enumeration tag names are deliberately not aliased with #define:
several of them collide with struct member names, and a macro would
silently rewrite call->clip_validity. The handful of 'enum <name>' uses
are renamed instead. drivers/isimodem is left alone, since it has its
own unrelated call_status and network_registration_status enumerations.

Values are unchanged; a generated set of 43 static assertions against
the pristine tree confirms it. OFONO_GPRS_AUTH_METHOD_ANY is appended
rather than inserted, so the existing auth method values keep their
meaning, and is handled in the two switches that enumerate the type.

struct ofono_debug_desc gains a notify callback and OFONO_DEBUG_ATTR, so
a plugin can place a descriptor in the __debug section and be told when
ofonod -d enables it. Without the call in log.c the plugin's own log
control would compile but never fire.

(cherry picked from commit b506385c9ade063316e28b3bbfc1fd79c076c296)
